Γöé  Returns HTML dashboard interface for monitoring load balancer behavior.    Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ---                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ## ≡ƒº¬ API Testing Strategies                                               Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Manual Testing Approaches**                                          Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **1. Postman Collection Testing**                                     Γöé
Γöé  - **Tool**: Postman GUI                                                    Γöé
Γöé  - **Benefits**: Visual interface, easy request building                    Γöé
Γöé  - **Scenarios**: CRUD operations, validation testing, error handling       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **2. Browser-Based Testing**                                          Γöé
Γöé  - **Tool**: Web browser for GET endpoints                                  Γöé
Γöé  - **Benefits**: Quick verification, visual response inspection             Γöé
Γöé  - **Scenarios**: Health checks, data retrieval endpoints                   Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **3. cURL Command Testing**                                           Γöé
Γöé  - **Tool**: Command line cURL                                              Γöé
Γöé  - **Benefits**: Scriptable, automation-ready                               Γöé
Γöé  - **Scenarios**: CI/CD integration, batch testing                          Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Automated Testing Approaches**                                       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **1. Unit Testing (NUnit)**                                           Γöé
Γöé  ```csharp                                                                  Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public async Task GetCities_Should_ReturnAllCities()                       Γöé
Γöé  {                                                                          Γöé
Γöé      // Arrange                                                             Γöé
Γöé      var client = _factory.CreateClient();                                  Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Act                                                                 Γöé
Γöé      var response = await client.GetAsync("/api/cities");                   Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Assert                                                              Γöé
Γöé      response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();                                    Γöé
Γöé      var content = await response.Content.ReadAsStringAsync();              Γöé
Γöé      var result = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<CitiesResponse>(content);      Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      Assert.That(result.Cities.Count, Is.GreaterThan(0));                   Γöé
Γöé      Assert.That(result.ServedBy, Is.Not.Null);                             Γöé
Γöé  }                                                                          Γöé
Γöé  ```                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **2. Integration Testing**                                            Γöé
Γöé  ```csharp                                                                  Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public async Task CreateCity_Should_PersistData()                          Γöé
Γöé  {                                                                          Γöé
Γöé      // Arrange                                                             Γöé
Γöé      var client = _factory.CreateClient();                                  Γöé
Γöé      var cityRequest = new { name = "Test City", country = "Test Country"   Γöé
Γöé  };                                                                         Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Act                                                                 Γöé
Γöé      var response = await client.PostAsJsonAsync("/api/cities",             Γöé
Γöé  cityRequest);                                                              Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Assert                                                              Γöé
Γöé      response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();                                    Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Verify persistence                                                  Γöé
Γöé      var getResponse = await client.GetAsync("/api/cities");                Γöé
Γöé      var cities = await                                                     Γöé
Γöé  getResponse.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<CitiesResponse>();                   Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      Assert.That(cities.Cities.Any(c => c.Name == "Test City"), Is.True);   Γöé
Γöé  }                                                                          Γöé
Γöé  ```                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **3. API Contract Testing**                                           Γöé
Γöé  - **Schema Validation**: Ensure response matches expected schema           Γöé
Γöé  - **Status Code Testing**: Verify appropriate HTTP status codes            Γöé
Γöé  - **Header Validation**: Check response headers and content types          Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ---                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ## ≡ƒôè Manual vs Automated Testing Comparison                               Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  | Testing Aspect | Manual Approach | Automated Approach |                  Γöé
Γöé  |----------------|-----------------|-------------------|                   Γöé
Γöé  | **Request Creation** | Postman GUI | HttpClient + JSON |                 Γöé
Γöé  | **Response Validation** | Visual inspection | Assert statements |        Γöé
Γöé  | **Data Verification** | Manual database checks | Automated queries |     Γöé
Γöé  | **Error Testing** | Manual invalid inputs | Parameterized tests |        Γöé
Γöé  | **Performance Testing** | Manual timing | Automated benchmarks |         Γöé
Γöé  | **Regression Testing** | Manual re-testing | Automated test suites |     Γöé
Γöé  | **Load Testing** | Manual multiple requests | Automated load generators  Γöé
Γöé  |                                                                          Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Transition Path**                                                    Γöé
Γöé  1. **Start with Manual**: Use Postman for understanding API behavior       Γöé
Γöé  2. **Document Scenarios**: Record test cases and expected results          Γöé
Γöé  3. **Automate High-Value Tests**: Convert frequent tests to automation     Γöé
Γöé  4. **Build Test Suites**: Create comprehensive automated test coverage     Γöé
Γöé  5. **Integrate CI/CD**: Include tests in deployment pipeline               Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ---                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ## ≡ƒöì Error Handling Patterns                                              Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Standard Error Response Format**                                     Γöé
Γöé  ```json                                                                    Γöé
Γöé  {                                                                          Γöé
Γöé    "error": "Human-readable error message",                                 Γöé
Γöé    "instance": "api-instance-identifier",                                   Γöé
Γöé    "timestamp": "2025-09-21T10:30:00Z",                                     Γöé
Γöé    "validationErrors": ["Detailed validation messages"]                     Γöé
Γöé  }                                                                          Γöé
Γöé  ```                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **HTTP Status Codes Used**                                             Γöé
Γöé  - **200 OK**: Successful GET, PUT, DELETE operations                       Γöé
Γöé  - **201 Created**: Successful POST operations                              Γöé
Γöé  - **400 Bad Request**: Validation errors, invalid input                    Γöé
Γöé  - **404 Not Found**: Resource not found                                    Γöé
Γöé  - **409 Conflict**: Duplicate resources, constraint violations             Γöé
Γöé  - **500 Internal Server Error**: Server errors, database issues            Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Error Testing Scenarios**                                            Γöé
Γöé  - Γ£à **Input Validation**: Test all required fields and formats            Γöé
Γöé  - Γ£à **Resource Not Found**: Test with non-existent IDs                    Γöé
Γöé  - Γ£à **Duplicate Detection**: Test unique constraint violations            Γöé
Γöé  - Γ£à **Foreign Key Validation**: Test invalid references                   Γöé
Γöé  - Γ£à **Server Error Handling**: Test database connection failures          Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ---                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ## ≡ƒÜÇ Performance Considerations                                           Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Load Balancing Benefits**                                            Γöé
Γöé  - **Multiple Instances**: Requests distributed across API instances        Γöé
Γöé  - **Database Sharing**: Consistent data across all instances               Γöé
Γöé  - **Instance Identification**: Response tracking for debugging             Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Optimization Features**                                              Γöé
Γöé  - **Result Limiting**: Weather endpoints limited to 50 records             Γöé
Γöé  - **Efficient Queries**: Optimized Entity Framework queries                Γöé
Γöé  - **Soft Deletes**: Logical deletion for data integrity                    Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Performance Testing Endpoints**                                      Γöé
Γöé  - **High-Volume Data**: Weather endpoints for load testing                 Γöé
Γöé  - **Database Operations**: All CRUD operations for stress testing          Γöé
Γöé  - **Health Monitoring**: Health check endpoint for uptime monitoring       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
