Γöé  ## ≡ƒôè Manual vs Automated Testing Comparison                               Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Testing Approach Comparison**                                        Γöé
Γöé  ![alt text](../Diagrams/manual-vs-automated-testing-flow.svg)              Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Comparison Table**                                                   Γöé
Γöé  | Testing Aspect | Manual Approach | Automated Approach | Transition       Γöé
Γöé  Benefits |                                                                 Γöé
Γöé  |----------------|-----------------|-------------------|-----------------  Γöé
Γöé  --|                                                                        Γöé
Γöé  | **≡ƒöä Repeatability** | Manual repetition required | Automated            Γöé
Γöé  repetition | Consistent execution |                                        Γöé
Γöé  | **ΓÜí Speed** | Slow (minutes per test) | Fast (seconds per test) |       Γöé
Γöé  Rapid feedback |                                                           Γöé
Γöé  | **≡ƒôè Coverage** | Limited by time | Extensive coverage possible |        Γöé
Γöé  Better quality |                                                           Γöé
Γöé  | **≡ƒº¬ Data Setup** | Manual database setup | Automated test data |        Γöé
Γöé  Reliable state |                                                           Γöé
Γöé  | **Γ£à Verification** | Visual inspection | Automated assertions |         Γöé
Γöé  Precise validation |                                                       Γöé
Γöé  | **≡ƒôê Reporting** | Manual documentation | Automated reports | Detailed   Γöé
Γöé  insights |                                                                 Γöé
Γöé  | **≡ƒöº Maintenance** | No code maintenance | Test code updates |           Γöé
Γöé  Long-term efficiency |                                                     Γöé
Γöé  | **≡ƒÆ░ Cost** | High ongoing effort | Low ongoing cost | ROI improvement   Γöé
Γöé  |                                                                          Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ---                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ## ∩┐╜ Test Naming Standards                                                 Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Overview**                                                           Γöé
Γöé  Test naming standards are crucial for creating maintainable, readable,     Γöé
Γöé  and self-documenting test suites. Well-named tests serve as living         Γöé
Γöé  documentation that clearly communicates the expected behavior of your      Γöé
Γöé  system.                                                                    Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Common Test Naming Conventions**                                     Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  Let's examine different naming standards using the same test scenario:     Γöé
Γöé  *Testing city creation with an empty name should return a validation       Γöé
Γöé  error*.                                                                    Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **1. GivenA_WhenB_ThenC Pattern (CURRENT STANDARD)**                  Γöé
Γöé  **Format**: `GivenA[Context]_When[Action]_Then[ExpectedResult]`            Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  **Why This Standard?**                                                     Γöé
Γöé  - **Γ£à Clear Structure**: Maps directly to Arrange-Act-Assert pattern      Γöé
Γöé  - **Γ£à Business Language**: Uses domain terminology that business          Γöé
Γöé  stakeholders understand                                                    Γöé
Γöé  - **Γ£à Comprehensive**: Captures context, action, and expected outcome     Γöé
Γöé  - **Γ£à Searchable**: Easy to find tests for specific scenarios             Γöé
Γöé  - **Γ£à Self-Documenting**: Test name explains the entire scenario          Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ```csharp                                                                  Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void                                                                Γöé
Γöé  GivenAnEmptyCityName_WhenCreatingCity_ThenValidationErrorShouldBeReturned  Γöé
Γöé  ()                                                                         Γöé
Γöé  {                                                                          Γöé
Γöé      // Arrange (Given)                                                     Γöé
Γöé      var request = new CreateCityRequest { Name = "", Country = "Test       Γöé
Γöé  Country" };                                                                Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Act (When)                                                          Γöé
Γöé      var result = await _controller.AddCity(request);                       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Assert (Then)                                                       Γöé
Γöé      result.Result.Should().BeOfType<BadRequestObjectResult>();             Γöé
Γöé  }                                                                          Γöé
Γöé  ```                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  **Pros**: Excellent traceability to requirements, maps to AAA pattern,     Γöé
Γöé  business-friendly language                                                 Γöé
Γöé  **Cons**: Can result in longer test names, requires discipline to          Γöé
Γöé  maintain consistency                                                       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **2. Should_ExpectedBehavior_When_StateUnderTest Pattern**            Γöé
Γöé  **Format**: `Should_[ExpectedBehavior]_When_[StateUnderTest]`              Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ```csharp                                                                  Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void Should_ReturnValidationError_When_CityNameIsEmpty()            Γöé
Γöé  {                                                                          Γöé
Γöé      // Arrange                                                             Γöé
Γöé      var request = new CreateCityRequest { Name = "", Country = "Test       Γöé
Γöé  Country" };                                                                Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Act                                                                 Γöé
Γöé      var result = await _controller.AddCity(request);                       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Assert                                                              Γöé
Γöé      result.Result.Should().BeOfType<BadRequestObjectResult>();             Γöé
Γöé  }                                                                          Γöé
Γöé  ```                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  **Pros**: Simple, focuses on expected behavior                             Γöé
Γöé  **Cons**: Less context about initial state, can become verbose             Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **3. MethodName_Scenario_ExpectedResult Pattern**                     Γöé
Γöé  **Format**: `[MethodName]_[Scenario]_[ExpectedResult]`                     Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ```csharp                                                                  Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void AddCity_WithEmptyName_ReturnsBadRequest()                      Γöé
Γöé  {                                                                          Γöé
Γöé      // Arrange                                                             Γöé
Γöé      var request = new CreateCityRequest { Name = "", Country = "Test       Γöé
Γöé  Country" };                                                                Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Act                                                                 Γöé
Γöé      var result = await _controller.AddCity(request);                       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Assert                                                              Γöé
Γöé      result.Result.Should().BeOfType<BadRequestObjectResult>();             Γöé
Γöé  }                                                                          Γöé
Γöé  ```                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  **Pros**: Clear method being tested                                        Γöé
Γöé  **Cons**: Tied to implementation, harder to refactor                       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **4. Sentence-Style Naming**                                          Γöé
Γöé  **Format**: Natural language sentences                                     Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ```csharp                                                                  Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void Creating_a_city_with_empty_name_returns_validation_error()     Γöé
Γöé  {                                                                          Γöé
Γöé      // Arrange                                                             Γöé
Γöé      var request = new CreateCityRequest { Name = "", Country = "Test       Γöé
Γöé  Country" };                                                                Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Act                                                                 Γöé
Γöé      var result = await _controller.AddCity(request);                       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé      // Assert                                                              Γöé
Γöé      result.Result.Should().BeOfType<BadRequestObjectResult>();             Γöé
Γöé  }                                                                          Γöé
Γöé  ```                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  **Pros**: Very readable, natural language                                  Γöé
Γöé  **Cons**: Can become very long, inconsistent formatting                    Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Test Name Quality Guidelines**                                       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **Essential Elements**                                                Γöé
Γöé  1. **Context (Given)**: What is the initial state or setup?                Γöé
Γöé  2. **Action (When)**: What operation is being performed?                   Γöé
Γöé  3. **Outcome (Then)**: What should happen as a result?                     Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **Best Practices**                                                    Γöé
Γöé  ```csharp                                                                  Γöé
Γöé  // Γ£à GOOD - Clear, specific, follows GivenA_WhenB_ThenC                   Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void                                                                Γöé
Γöé  GivenANonExistentCityId_WhenGettingWeatherData_ThenNotFoundShouldBeReturn  Γöé
Γöé  ed()                                                                       Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  // Γ¥î POOR - Vague, doesn't indicate expected behavior                     Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void TestWeatherApi()                                               Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  // Γ¥î POOR - Focuses on implementation, not behavior                       Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void GetWeatherByCity_Test()                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  // Γ¥î POOR - Missing context about the scenario                            Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void Should_ReturnNotFound()                                        Γöé
Γöé  ```                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **Naming Anti-Patterns to Avoid**                                     Γöé
Γöé  ```csharp                                                                  Γöé
Γöé  // Γ¥î Generic test names                                                   Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void Test1() { }                                                    Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void TestMethod() { }                                               Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  // Γ¥î Implementation-focused names                                         Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void CallsRepository() { }                                          Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void MockReturnsNull() { }                                          Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  // Γ¥î Unclear expected outcomes                                            Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void WeatherTest_Something() { }                                    Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void Should_Work() { }                                              Γöé
Γöé  ```                                                                        Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  ### **Domain-Specific Naming Examples**                                    Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  #### **Weather API Tests**                                                 Γöé
Γöé  ```csharp                                                                  Γöé
Γöé  // Unit Tests                                                              Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void                                                                Γöé
Γöé  GivenAValidTemperature_WhenCreatingWeather_ThenWeatherShouldHaveCorrectTe  Γöé
Γöé  mperature()                                                                Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void                                                                Γöé
Γöé  GivenANegativeWindSpeed_WhenValidatingWeather_ThenValidationErrorShouldBe  Γöé
Γöé  Raised()                                                                   Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  // Integration Tests                                                       Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void                                                                Γöé
Γöé  GivenAnExistingCity_WhenPostingWeatherData_ThenWeatherShouldBeSavedToData  Γöé
Γöé  base()                                                                     Γöé
Γöé                                                                             Γöé
Γöé  [Test]                                                                     Γöé
Γöé  public void                                                                Γöé
